{"id":2012,"date":"2014-09-24T21:09:23","date_gmt":"2014-09-24T21:09:23","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/?p=2012"},"modified":"2017-10-20T11:19:38","modified_gmt":"2017-10-20T17:19:38","slug":"charles-debugging-proxy-genymotion","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/charles-debugging-proxy-genymotion\/","title":{"rendered":"Charles Debugging Proxy &#038; Genymotion"},"content":{"rendered":"<p>I&#8217;ve been using <a title=\"Charles Debugging Proxy\" href=\"https:\/\/www.charlesproxy.com\/\" target=\"_blank\">Charles Debugging Proxy<\/a>\u00a0for almost 8 years to help with debugging server side issues. It is a great tool that makes testing easier in many ways:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Seeing server requests &amp; responses<\/li>\n<li>Mapping a local file to replace the response from the server for testing purposes<\/li>\n<li>Testing file sizes of web or app assets<\/li>\n<li>Checking server response durations<\/li>\n<li>Simulate slower connection speeds<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>Lately I&#8217;ve been using Charles during iPhone and Android app testing. It makes it so much easier for me to determine if a bug is app related or server related. The benefit of this is that I can reduce the turnaround time for a fix since I can provide a better description of the issue and assign it to the correct team member.<\/p>\n<p>A friend, John Blanco, turned me onto <a title=\"Genymotion\" href=\"https:\/\/www.genymotion.com\/\" target=\"_blank\">Genymotion<\/a>\u00a0recently. It is by far my favorite Android emulator. When combining Charles and Genymotion together it has greatly simplified my testing efforts for an Android app that I&#8217;ve been testing. I can drag a .apk file onto Genymotion and run it quickly with ease. There are a few tricks to get Charles to play nice with Genymotion:<br \/>\nIn your Genymotion Android emulator\u2026<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Settings -> Wifi -> Press and hold your active network<\/li>\n<li>Select \u201cModify Network\u201d<\/li>\n<li>Select \u201cShow Advanced Options\u201d<\/li>\n<li>Select \u201cProxy Settings -> Manual\u201d<\/li>\n<li>Set your Proxy to: 10.0.3.2 (Genymotion\u2019s special code for the local workstation)<\/li>\n<li>Set your Port to: 8888<\/li>\n<li>Press Save<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>I&#8217;ve been using Charles Debugging Proxy\u00a0for almost 8 years to help with debugging server side issues. It is a great tool that makes testing easier in many ways: Seeing server requests &amp; responses Mapping a local file to replace the response from the server for testing purposes Testing file sizes of web or app assets&#8230;<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":2016,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"footnotes":""},"categories":[28,27,24,29],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-2012","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-charles-proxy","category-debugging","category-defects","category-genymotion"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/2012","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=2012"}],"version-history":[{"count":5,"href":"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/2012\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":2102,"href":"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/2012\/revisions\/2102"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/2016"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=2012"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"category","embeddable":t